        "description": "<img src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/directive-8020-header.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp\" /> <p>Supermassive's \"party horror\" games, as I like to call them, have become a guilty pleasure of mine. This series famously began with <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/until-dawn-review\">Until Dawn in 2015</a> and peaked with <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/house-of-ashes-review-the-dark-picture-anthologys-best-entry-yet\">House of Ashes in 2021</a>, if you ask me. (Although I enjoyed the schlocky <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/the-quarry-review-sumptuous-slasher-horror-digs-its-own-grave\">Quarry in 2022</a> as well.) It's a series pitched like an interactive horror movie, where you try to shepherd a group of ill-fated characters through a slasher by making various important choices for them, hoping they don't get shredded as a result.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/directive-8020-dark-pictures-preview\">Read more</a></p>",
